{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Defined in trust_but_verify.\n/// Application data and operations used to evaluate criteria.\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.domain` has two obligations. Every application domain implements `trust_but_verify::Domain`, and a domain is cloneable and safe to share between executions. The trait is declared as `Clone + Send + Sync`. The \"chapters introduce its members\" sentence only orients the reader and adds no testable obligation.\n\n**Bound on the trait.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` defines an opaque `Relationships` type and implements `Domain` for it. It then compiles generic code against the declared bound:\n- `check_bounds::<G: Domain>` calls `domain::<G>()`, whose bound is `T: Clone + Send + Sync`. This fails to compile if `Domain` stops implying `Clone`, `Send` or `Sync`.\n- `Relationships` itself derives `Clone` and implements `Domain`, so the test also shows that an application type can implement the trait.\n- The test calls the trait methods on the instance and asserts their results.\n\n**Sharing between executions.** Several tests clone or share one domain across concurrent executions and assert the outcomes:\n- `contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]` builds a `Validator` from `domain.clone()`. It runs two verifications concurrently and asserts that each keeps its own output, revision and dependencies.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` runs three concurrent verifications against a cloned `Memory` domain. It asserts that the executions overlap (`peak == 3`) and that their traces stay separate.\n- `agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]` and `validation.rs#fn[shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls]` share one graph reference between concurrent agent calls.\n\n**Implements `Domain`.** `contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]`, `agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` and `agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]` use `Domain` implementations through `Validator::new(domain.clone())`. This confirms the validator accepts them as the trait and clones them.\n\nI found no gap: the compile-time bound check and the concurrent sharing tests cover both obligations.",
  "references": "ed9ccc46ca7c14b9cdfc7ded9a2564da2295f3d6c8694a892bc5e88cc71c5a03",
